  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICNL: Partners in Enabling Environment Reform (PEER)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partners in Enabling Environment Reform (PEER) will help address this challenge, empowering civil society to address legal issues that shrink or shift civic space.
PEER will enhance civil society&apos;s influence on legal dimensions of civic space in Norway&apos;s partner countries. Specifically, PEER will support civil society coordination and collaboration; increase expertise on civil society legal issues; facilitate dialogue with government; engage with multilateral bodies to influence state conduct; and promote political systems thinking. PEER will enhance civil society&apos;s literacy and capacity to shape the digital environment for civic space. PEER will share learning among partners on successful strategies and tactics to protect civic space in various contexts. And PEER will provide rapid assistance to enhance civil society&apos;s readiness for the emergence of reform opportunities or restrictions on civic space.
PEER will be focus on ten priority countries, including Colombia, Ethiopia, Indonesia, Malawi, Mozambique, Myanmar, Nepal, Palestine, Tanzania, and Uganda. Civil society partners in each country will lead implementation efforts, with ICNL&apos;s technical and financial support. PEER will also enable rapid response assistance to empower civil society readiness in the face of sudden shifts in civic space, whether opportunities for improvement or threats to the legal environment.
Through PEER, civil society in priority countries will be better able to counter closing civic space by enhancing protection and better placed to influence law and policy affecting civic space, thereby advancing a more enabling legal environment for civic space.</narrative>
  </description>
